<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Defs>
  <!--
    The Hemophage's shell, on VFEP's armor base (VFEP v4.03,
    1.6/Defs/ThingDefs_Misc/Apparel_Various.xml). Docs/Research/VFEP_WARCASKET_STATS.md
    tabulates the tier.

    Tuning: the 10th generation's baseline but for the heat plating, the blood pumping floor
    and the hemogen packs. Each field is the value most of VFEP's five spacer sets
    (Siegebreaker, Guardian, Controller, Sarcophagus, Brute) share, which is the
    Sarcophagus's row less its glitterworld medicine and its bionics. With the bionics go
    its guards against downing and death and all but one of its capacity floors of 1: the
    0.7 floors on Moving and Manipulation below are the other four sets'.
    - Sharp 2 / Blunt 1 on the armor and the shoulders. Blunt 1.5 is the Guardian's and the
      Brute's specialty, which the helmet alone takes, with Heat 2 (its header).
    - Heat 1.5 on the armor and the shoulders, over the tier's 1. Flame damage arrives
      without armor penetration, so 1 stops half of it and halves the rest, and 1.5 stops
      three quarters. Biotech's FireWeakness gene, the sanguophage's, multiplies flame damage
      by 4 before armor: at 1 its carrier burns about as an unarmored baseliner does, at 1.5
      about half as fast. The Hazard's 2 on every piece would stop all of it and leave the
      gene nothing; it stays that set's, with its Flammability 0. Catching fire is the
      pawn's Flammability, which nothing here changes.
    - EnergyShieldEnergyMax 1.5 at EnergyShieldRechargeRate 0.01 (Guardian, Controller,
      Sarcophagus). Siegebreaker's 2.5 and the Brute's 5.0 are their specialties. The bubble
      is the tier's plain one, blocking ranged attacks only.
    - PsychicSensitivity -0.5, ToxicResistance 0.5, SlaveSuppressionOffset 0.3 and
      VacuumResistance 0.2, the same on all five.
    - costList ComponentSpacer 6 / Plasteel 145 / Uranium 50, the Siegebreaker's and the
      Sarcophagus's. The components are VFEP's tech-complexity dial (Brute 4, Controller 12),
      the plasteel runs 145 to 200 across the tier. DevilstrandCloth 50 pays for the heat
      plating in the Hazard's currency, half of that armor's 100 for half its step, as 25 on
      the shoulders is half of its shoulders' 50.
    - HemogenPack 5 primes the injectors, the count each of Biotech's deathrest buildings
      takes. A pack does not spoil, the foundry welds any costList item, and like the rest
      of the cost none comes back.
    - BloodPumping floor 1, the one floor of the Sarcophagus's kept: the injectors move the
      pilot's blood whatever the heart does. VEF lifts the finished capacity, a destroyed
      heart's 0 included (its PawnCapacityUtility.CalculateCapacityLevel postfix), and death
      by a lost capacity asks for that level. So in the armor a lost heart neither kills a
      pilot nor puts a Deathless one into the coma that stands in for death
      (SanguophageUtility.ShouldBeDeathrestingOrInComaInsteadOfDead asks ShouldBeDead first;
      1.6), and nothing that lowers blood pumping slows them. Any pilot has it, hemogenic or
      not, as any has the heat plating, and out of the armor the heart counts again. The
      hemogen rush raises blood pumping over this (HediffDefs/HemogenRush.xml).
    - researchPrerequisites VFEP_SpacerWarcaskets, the tier's. The foundry lists a part by
      BuildableDef.IsResearchFinished, which wants every entry, so a second prerequisite
      would go on all three pieces.

    No apparel tags, so no pawnkind's gear roll picks the set (PawnApparelGenerator matches a
    kind's apparelTags against them), where the tier's WarcasketVeteran and WarcasketAll
    would put it on VFEP's veteran raiders and hired veterans: a generated pilot is rarely
    hemogenic, and VEF fires no apparel ability's autocast, so a raider casts neither the
    rush nor Dismember and the set arrives as a plain spacer warcasket. VFEP's slot fill
    reads no tags; Source/1.6/Patches/PawnGenerator_GeneratePawn_Patch_Postfix.cs keeps the
    set out of it. Save Our Ship 2's EVA tag (1.6/Patches/SOS2Patch.xml) is then the only one
    a part has. The generated pawns that may wear the set are dressed after generation
    (Quest pilots, below).

    Quest pilots: QuestPilotExtension, the set on the sanguophages Biotech's two sanguophage
    quests generate, hemogenic by their pawn kind and so the pilots the set is built for.
    Source/1.6/QuestPilot/QuestPilot.cs has how a pawn is dressed. A set that arrives this
    way cannot be taken off and reused (VFEP blocks the strip and the drop), so what the
    player can gain from it is the pilot inside. The three chances, shipMasterMinPoints and
    requiredResearch are mod settings defaulting to the values here:
    - meetingLeaderChance 0.6, the sanguophage who asks for the meeting and leads it: a
      neutral guest, so most meetings show the set without setting it against the colony.
      The leader is also the one who may offer to join, one of the two or three turns the
      quest draws from mid-meeting, and then brings the set along.
    - meetingGuestChance 0.1, each of the one to seven others: now and then a second set at
      the table, and a betrayed meeting that is rarely much harder than vanilla's.
    - shipMasterChance 0. The master of the crashed shuttle is that quest's prize, to be
      downed and captured, and the set closes most of the ways to down one: the trait's
      zero pain ends pain shock, the three pieces' PsychicSensitivity sums to -1.2, a
      sanguophage's whole 120%, so a psychic weapon reaches only a pilot whose trait raises
      it, and the floors below hold Moving and Manipulation.
      The quest sizes its thralls from threat points that count none of this.
    - shipMasterMinPoints 2500, the quest's threat points the master's chance needs. The
      quest spends its points on head count alone: the master plus thralls from two curves,
      (0, 2) to (2000, 5) in the shuttle and (2000, 0), (2500, 2), (5000, 4), (8000, 6)
      dropped later, every pawn at combatPower 100. So vanilla's quest is a whole raid's
      worth of combat power at its 300-point floor and about a third of one at 2500. The set
      is priced at about 450 combat power on top of the master's 100, an estimate from VFEP's
      own warcasket pilots (300 to 600 against 65 to 220 for its kinds without one). At 2500
      the dressed quest is 1250 combat power, half a raid at those points, and it is the
      first of the slider's stops at which the quest brings two reinforcements (one arrives
      from just over 2125 points, two from 2375). Under the floor the master is never
      dressed, whatever the chance. 0 is no floor. Unlike the chance, the floor answers the
      fight's size, not the capture: a dressed master is as hard to down at any points.
    - requiredResearch VFEP_Warcaskets, the player's own, read as the quest is generated:
      a colony that has not opened VFEP's warcasket line meets none of these pilots.
      researchOptions are the steps the settings offer after "none", the four of VFEP's
      warcasket line in the order its prerequisites chain them, ending on the set's own
      VFEP_SpacerWarcaskets.
    - otherPieces, with this def the set a pilot is dressed in, all of it or none.
    - rangedWeapon VFEP_WarcasketGun_Autorifle and meleeWeapon
      VFEP_WarcasketMeleeWeapon_Broadsword, what a dressed pawn's own weapon is exchanged
      for, in either quest and in any set: the two plain weapons of VFEP's line (the
      autorifle is the one its footsoldiers carry), so a pawn in a warcasket fights as VFEP's
      own pilots do and the prices below, which are VFEP's for armed pilots, hold. A
      sanguophage takes the one that fits the higher of their Shooting and Melee, a thrall
      the kind of weapon they held. A meeting's leader who joins brings the weapon along.

    The crashed shuttle's thralls, on the same extension: some of them arrive in one of VFEP's
    two plain sets, which have no module for the AI to leave unused. Source/1.6/QuestPilot/
    ThrallBudget.cs has the rule and QuestPilot.cs the order they are dressed in.
    - thrallBudgetShare 0.25, a mod setting: the dressed quest is worth a quarter of a raid at
      the same threat points, where vanilla's is 32% of one at 2500 points and 12% at 10000.
      With the master undressed the share alone dresses one thrall from 5000 points, two
      from 7000, three of the eleven at 8000 and five at 10000, so the master's escort stays
      a mix and the quest stays a chance to capture the master and never a raid. On by default where the master's own chance is
      off: dressed thralls leave the master as easy to down as vanilla does.
    - thrallMinPoints 2500 and thrallMinDressed 1: from 2500 points one thrall is dressed
      whatever the share leaves, since a flat share shows no warcasket before 5000. At 2500 the
      quest is then 1000 combat power, 40% of a raid, under the half a raid the master's own
      floor allows at the same points, and it is where the quest first has reinforcements for
      the set to arrive with.
    - shipMasterPrice 450, the estimate above, which the budget pays before any thrall while
      the master is dressed.
    - thrallTiers, each set with its price in combat power over a thrall's own 100:
      VFEP_Warcasket at 200, VFEP's own VFEP_Footsoldier (combatPower 300, this set and a
      WarcasketBasic weapon) less the thrall, and Marine at 250. VFEP prices no pawn for the
      Marine set alone (VFEP_Veteran, 400, draws either set and dearer weapons), and it is the
      same shell with about an eighth more armor, so it is priced a quarter over the basic set
      and not at the Veteran's 300. Each set needs its own armor's research of the player.

    Hemogen rush: the armor's module, a toggled ability granted by the CompAbilitiesApparel
    below. AbilityDefs/HemogenRush.xml and HediffDefs/HemogenRush.xml have it.

    Text: the shape is l10n/languages/English.md's VFE Pirates recipe: a first line that is
    also the shortDescription and names the piece's module, a generation paragraph, then the
    series paragraph. The second and third paragraphs are identical in all three defs. The
    second is ours, where the recipe pastes VFEP's verbatim: VFEP's paragraph gives the
    generation to a government program for its veterans, and this set's fiction is that
    sanguophages inside that program had it built in secret for themselves, told as rumor
    the way Biotech tells its sanguophage lore. Its first sentence is the Medic's and the
    Overlord's telling of the program, with the generation as its subject, so the set is
    never called the program's own. The rumor is two, one belief set against another as
    Biotech's xenotype text sets them ("Some think ...", "Some believe ..."), and neither is
    settled. The third says what each piece does in VFEP's functional voice and ends on
    VFEP's verdict of who the series suits; the tier's sets carry no catchphrase. A whole
    description stays inside the 133 to 205 words of VFEP's spacer sets and the siblings'.

    What the text may say of hemogen is what Biotech says: a hemogenic's own is in stores in
    the body ("internal hemogen stores", "hemogen glands"), never in the blood, and blood is
    what hemogen is extracted from. So the suit spends the pilot's hemogen, and the pilot
    drains hemogen from a wound, which says where it comes from and not how. The pads have
    no hardware for the drain: their servos and reinforced arms tear the limb, and the rest
    is the pilot's own. Any hemogenic pilot drains (AbilityDefs/Dismember.xml), so the text
    names neither fangs nor Bloodfeed, which are the bloodfeeder gene's, nor feeding, which
    reads as eating.

    Art: Textures/Things/Pawn/Warcasketlike/WarcasketHemophage/, laid out as VFEP's sets are.
    The worn graphic is Graphic_Multi (the _north/_east/_south facings); the item icon is the
    parent's Graphic_Single, read from the bare-named file, a copy of the _south facing.

    Masked tint, all three pieces (of VFEP's sets only the helmets are masked; vanilla's
    prestige armors are the pattern): CutoutComplex on both graphics of each piece, the worn one through
    apparel.useWornGraphicMask, so the CompColorable colour paints the mask's red areas and
    the black-masked parts keep their painted red (apparel graphics pass white as colorTwo).
    Mask names differ by graphic class: Graphic_Multi reads <path>_northm, Graphic_Single
    <path>_m.

    Glow: WarcasketHemophageGlow_north/_east/_south beside the art (and the helmet's and
    shoulders' under their own names) are white shapes over the red details that light up.
    They are drawn to the art, not to the masks: on the shell and the helmet they cover the
    black-masked parts with a margin, on the pads only the red of the servo pistons. Each piece's
    renderNodeProperties entry draws its own sprite, tinted by color, while the pilot has
    the hemogen rush hediff (PawnRenderNode_HemogenGlow). parentTagDef is the tag the game
    parents that piece's worn sprite to, ApparelBody here and on the pads, ApparelHead on
    the helmet; the node finds the sprite among that parent's children. TransparentPostLight
    so the glow reads at night.

    Traits: traitsOnEquip grants HPWC_WarcasketTrait_Hemophage in place of
    VFEP_WarcasketTrait, since a child ApparelExtension can only add to what a granted trait
    blocks and the suit leaves its pilot intellectual work (TraitDefs/
    WarcasketTrait_Hemophage.xml). traitsOnUnequip keeps VFEP_Shellcasket, the "cut out of a
    warcasket" state every set shares, so removal surgery and re-entombing behave as for
    VFEP's own sets.

    ApparelExtension priority 1: VFEP_WarcasketArmorBase carries its own ApparelExtension and
    inheritance appends list items, so this def resolves with two. VEF merges duplicates in a
    Def.ResolveReferences prefix, the highest priority surviving, and ApparelExtension.Merge
    does not copy every field; at equal priority the parent's copy would win. At priority 1
    every field of ours, from any load root, is kept. Any new ApparelExtension field for this
    piece goes on this entry.

    Patched by 1.6/Patches/SOS2Patch.xml (EVA tag, cold insulation),
    1.6/Mods/VanillaGravshipExpanded/Patches/VacuumResistance.xml and the
    1.6/Mods/CombatExtended/Patches/ root (plating on CE's scale, bulk, carry capacity,
    shield, costs); see their headers.
  -->
  <VFEPirates.WarcasketDef ParentName="VFEP_WarcasketArmorBase">
    <defName>HPWC_Warcasket_Hemophage</defName>
    <label>hemophage warcasket</label>
    <shortDescription>Specialized spacer-tech warcasket shell with improved heat protection, equipped with hemogen injectors that replace the pilot's blood pumping and can spend hemogen to make them faster and stronger.</shortDescription>
    <description>Specialized spacer-tech warcasket shell with improved heat protection, equipped with hemogen injectors that replace the pilot's blood pumping and can spend hemogen to make them faster and stronger.\n\nThe 10th generation came out of a government program that rebuilt captured pirate rigs around its own power armor and gave them to veterans who could no longer serve any other way. The program has no record of a Hemophage series. Some think the designs were stolen and refitted by sanguophages. Some believe the series was sanctioned in secret from the top of the program, which sanguophages had directed all along.\n\nThe Hemophage series runs on its pilot's hemogen. Injectors in the shell keep the pilot's blood pumping even without a heart, and can spend their hemogen quickly to make them much faster and stronger. Servos in the pauldrons can tear a limb off an enemy so the pilot can drain hemogen from the wound, and the helmet keeps out sunlight and helps the pilot hold their nerve near fire. For a non-hemogenic pilot this series is somewhat lackluster, but it suits a sanguophage who prefers to fight up close.</description>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Pawn/Warcasketlike/WarcasketHemophage/WarcasketHemophage</texPath>
      <shaderType>CutoutComplex</shaderType>
    </graphicData>
    <statBases>
      <Mass>50</Mass>
      <ArmorRating_Sharp>2</ArmorRating_Sharp>
      <ArmorRating_Blunt>1</ArmorRating_Blunt>
      <ArmorRating_Heat>1.5</ArmorRating_Heat>
      <Insulation_Cold>80</Insulation_Cold>
      <Insulation_Heat>80</Insulation_Heat>
      <EquipDelay>1</EquipDelay>
      <EnergyShieldRechargeRate>0.01</EnergyShieldRechargeRate>
      <EnergyShieldEnergyMax>1.5</EnergyShieldEnergyMax>
    </statBases>
    <equippedStatOffsets>
      <PsychicSensitivity>-0.5</PsychicSensitivity>
      <ToxicResistance>0.5</ToxicResistance>
      <SlaveSuppressionOffset MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">0.3</SlaveSuppressionOffset>
      <VacuumResistance MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey">0.2</VacuumResistance>
    </equippedStatOffsets>
    <costList>
      <ComponentSpacer>6</ComponentSpacer>
      <Plasteel>145</Plasteel>
      <Uranium>50</Uranium>
      <DevilstrandCloth>50</DevilstrandCloth>
      <HemogenPack>5</HemogenPack>
    </costList>
    <researchPrerequisites>
      <li>VFEP_SpacerWarcaskets</li>
    </researchPrerequisites>
    <apparel>
      <bodyPartGroups>
        <li>Torso</li>
        <li>Legs</li>
        <li>Feet</li>
      </bodyPartGroups>
      <wornGraphicPath>Things/Pawn/Warcasketlike/WarcasketHemophage/WarcasketHemophage</wornGraphicPath>
      <useWornGraphicMask>true</useWornGraphicMask>
      <renderNodeProperties>
        <li>
          <debugLabel>HPWC_HemogenGlow</debugLabel>
          <nodeClass>HemophageWarcasket.PawnRenderNode_HemogenGlow</nodeClass>
          <workerClass>HemophageWarcasket.PawnRenderNodeWorker_HemogenGlow</workerClass>
          <parentTagDef>ApparelBody</parentTagDef>
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Warcasketlike/WarcasketHemophage/WarcasketHemophageGlow</texPath>
          <shaderTypeDef>TransparentPostLight</shaderTypeDef>
          <color>(1, 0.2, 0.15)</color>
        </li>
      </renderNodeProperties>
      <layers>
        <li>OnSkin</li>
        <li>Middle</li>
        <li>Shell</li>
      </layers>
    </apparel>
    <comps>
      <li Class="VEF.Apparels.CompProperties_ShieldBubble">
        <compClass>VEF.Apparels.CompShieldBubble</compClass>
        <blockRangedAttack>true</blockRangedAttack>
        <blockMeleeAttack>false</blockMeleeAttack>
        <showWhenDrafted>true</showWhenDrafted>
        <showOnHostiles>true</showOnHostiles>
        <showOnNeutralInCombat>true</showOnNeutralInCombat>
        <shieldTexPath>Other/ShieldBubble</shieldTexPath>
        <chargeFullyWhenMade>true</chargeFullyWhenMade>
        <minShieldSize>2.1</minShieldSize>
        <maxShieldSize>2.7</maxShieldSize>
        <disableRotation>true</disableRotation>
      </li>
      <li Class="VEF.Abilities.CompProperties_AbilitiesApparel">
        <abilities>
          <li>HPWC_HemogenRush</li>
        </abilities>
      </li>
    </comps>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="VEF.Apparels.ApparelExtension">
        <priority>1</priority>
        <traitsOnEquip>
          <li>HPWC_WarcasketTrait_Hemophage</li>
        </traitsOnEquip>
        <traitsOnUnequip>
          <li>VFEP_Shellcasket</li>
        </traitsOnUnequip>
        <pawnCapacityMinLevels>
          <li>
            <capacity>Moving</capacity>
            <minLevel>0.7</minLevel>
          </li>
          <li>
            <capacity>Manipulation</capacity>
            <minLevel>0.7</minLevel>
          </li>
          <li>
            <capacity>BloodPumping</capacity>
            <minLevel>1</minLevel>
          </li>
        </pawnCapacityMinLevels>
      </li>
      <li Class="HemophageWarcasket.QuestPilotExtension">
        <shipMasterChance>0</shipMasterChance>
        <shipMasterMinPoints>2500</shipMasterMinPoints>
        <meetingLeaderChance>0.6</meetingLeaderChance>
        <meetingGuestChance>0.1</meetingGuestChance>
        <requiredResearch>VFEP_Warcaskets</requiredResearch>
        <researchOptions>
          <li>VFEP_Warcaskets</li>
          <li>VFEP_AdvancedWarcaskets</li>
          <li>VFEP_SpecialisedWarcaskets</li>
          <li>VFEP_SpacerWarcaskets</li>
        </researchOptions>
        <otherPieces>
          <li>HPWC_WarcasketShoulders_Hemophage</li>
          <li>HPWC_WarcasketHelmet_Hemophage</li>
        </otherPieces>
        <rangedWeapon>VFEP_WarcasketGun_Autorifle</rangedWeapon>
        <meleeWeapon>VFEP_WarcasketMeleeWeapon_Broadsword</meleeWeapon>
        <thrallBudgetShare>0.25</thrallBudgetShare>
        <thrallMinPoints>2500</thrallMinPoints>
        <thrallMinDressed>1</thrallMinDressed>
        <shipMasterPrice>450</shipMasterPrice>
        <thrallTiers>
          <li>
            <armor>VFEP_Warcasket_Warcasket</armor>
            <otherPieces>
              <li>VFEP_WarcasketShoulders_Warcasket</li>
              <li>VFEP_WarcasketHelmet_Warcasket</li>
            </otherPieces>
            <price>200</price>
          </li>
          <li>
            <armor>VFEP_Warcasket_Marine</armor>
            <otherPieces>
              <li>VFEP_WarcasketShoulders_Marine</li>
              <li>VFEP_WarcasketHelmet_Marine</li>
            </otherPieces>
            <price>250</price>
          </li>
        </thrallTiers>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </VFEPirates.WarcasketDef>
</Defs>
